          "date_decided": "2012-05-04",
          "holding": "Reversing dismissal in substantial part, the court held that foster children stated substantive due process claims under both the special-relationship and state-created-danger doctrines, and separately analyzed which Child Welfare Act and CAPTA provisions create rights enforceable under § 1983.",
